\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Effect of maturation variability on different properties of the Godfray and Hassel 1989 model. In all subfigures, parameters are inspired from Xu et al. 2010 : $m_{H1} = 1/3, m_{H2} = 1/2, m_{H3} = 1/3, \delta _{H1} = \delta _{H2} = \delta _{H3} = 0, \delta _{H4} = 1, \delta _{P1} = 0, \delta _{P2} = 2.5, r = 15, a = 0.01, k = 1, ratioT = 1, n_1 = 50, n_2 = 50.$ \textbf  {(a)} : Non trivial equilibrium densities (noted $X^*$ for each stage X) as a function of $H_2$ and $P_1$ number of subcompartments $n_2 = m$ \textbf  {(b)} : Local stability boundaries taken from Xu et al. (2010) in the case of fixed delays for all stages. The stability boundaries are plotted with respect to the ratio of parasitoid to host generation times (ratioT) and the search aggregation parameter k. \textbf  {(c)} : Local stability boundaries for $n_2 = m = 3$ and various values of $(n_1,n_3)$ . For the stability curve on the right, all curves are perfectly superimposed such that only the one for $n_1 = n_3 = 500$ is drawn. \textbf  {(d)} : Local stability boundaries for $n_1 = n_3 = 300$ (except the grey curves taken from Xu et al. 2010 with fixed delays) related to the couples of characteristic roots responsible for the GC area at $ratioT \approx 1.5$. For clarity, the other "U" curves are not shown here.\relax }}{13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:Godfray}{{5}{13}}
